SM(461,{"n":"Acts 10","a":"Fr Stephen De Young Archives/Acts 10.mp3","d":2654.0,"s":[[0.16,"Come and study Holy Scriptures with us as Father Stephen DeYoung teaches verse by verse on the podcast The Whole Counsel of God."],[8.08,"Father Stephen is a former Protestant pastor and Bible teacher in the Reformed Church, but now an Orthodox priest serving at Archangel Gabriel Orthodox Church in Lafayette, Louisiana."],[21.04,"Okay, so we'll go ahead and get started, and when we get started in just a second, we're gonna be picking up in uh Acts of the Apostles, uh, chapter 10, verse 1."],[30.24,"Uh as I always mention, uh, by the time people are hearing this recording, the recording of the first uh Bible study on the book of Acts will be available for people to listen to too, so you can go back and listen to my introduction to the book."],[46.4,"But to sort of get us caught up to where we are right now, uh, in the Acts of the Apostles, where we're picking up, um we had read about how uh originally uh St."],[59.04,"Luke starts by. again telling us the story of Christ's ascension into heaven"],[63.96,"And he says to the disciples that they're going to be his witnesses in Jerusalem and then in all Judea and then Samaria and then to the ends of the earth."],[73.72,"And so we've seen already how that's sort of the plan that's been sort of unfolding in Acts as we go."],[81.24,"Most of the early chapters of Acts took place just in Jerusalem itself."],[88.44,"Even though the community was sort of growing and successful there, it hadn't really expanded much beyond Jerusalem, other than people who had come to Jerusalem, heard about Jesus, and then gone back home, you know, of course, taking it with them."],[103.72,"But then we saw the episode where uh Saint Stephen, one of the first deacons, had been uh stoned to death for his faith by the chief priests and the rulers of the people."],[116.48,"And uh after he had been stoned to death, that persecution that broke out sort of caused people to scatter a little bit."],[124.16,"So uh a lot of a lot of people then left Jerusalem, and that had the side effect, even though the intent, of course, of the people persecuting the Christians was to get rid of the Christians."],[136.08,"What it actually ended up doing is spreading Christianity sort of all over the countryside."],[140.24,"And we saw how St."],[141.2,"Philip, another one of the deacons, had uh preached in Samaria, and how he had uh preached to and uh helped convert uh by baptizing him, uh, an Ethiopian eunuch."],[156.2,"Uh and then in the last chapter, last time in chapter nine, uh, we saw Saul, who had Saul of Tarsus, who had been there uh at uh Saint Stephen's execution, sort of helping out, holding people's coats while they uh threw the stones, uh, how he had this encounter, he was on the the way to Damascus with uh letters of recommendation from the chief priests to try and root out the Christians there in Damascus and bring them back to Jerusalem to stand trial, but uh Christ himself appeared to him on the way and uh Saul was struck blind and ended up going to Damascus and um meeting the members of the Christian community there."],[204.56,"Uh one of them, St."],[205.6,"Ananias, baptized Saul and he received his sight back."],[210.88,"And uh Saul then, after spending some time there in Damascus, had to flee Damascus too, uh, because some of the people who were formerly his friends were now not his friends anymore."],[222.0,"And so he ended up being sort of let down through a window out of the wall, going to Jerusalem."],[228.8,"Uh when he got to Jerusalem, they weren't real sure about him either, because of course he had just recently been going around uh arresting and and uh killing Christians."],[240.6,"But eventually, due partially to the influence of Saint Barnabas, he had been sort of cautiously welcomed into the community."],[252.44,"And so at the very end of chapter 9, where we left off and where we're sort of going to be picking up this evening, we saw that Saint Peter also had sort of now moved out of Jerusalem at least a little bit to the countryside of Judea."],[270.28,"And he was going sort of from village to village and city to city."],[273.72,"And we saw that he, again, the very first thing that St."],[278.76,"Luke says at the beginning of the book of Acts is that in the gospel, according to St."],[283.88,"Luke, he had had uh described to us all the things that Jesus begun to do and teach."],[289.84,"So that the apostles are sort of continuing that now."],[292.96,"And we saw how Saint Peter uh was going from place to place, both doing the things that Jesus had done and healing the sick, including even raising a dead girl back to life, and also preaching uh about the kingdom of God in the way that Jesus had preached about the kingdom of God."],[312.48,"And so that's where we left off last time, and that's really where we're picking up this time at the beginning of chapter 10."],[318.64,"As we continue to talk about uh Saint Peter."],[323.28,"Um so, unless anybody has any questions or anything, we'll go ahead the leftover from before, we'll go ahead and start here. in Acts chapter 10, verse 1"],[335.88,"So there was a certain man in Caesarea named Cornelius, a centurion of what was called the Italian regiment."],[345.16,"So there are several Caesarea's, as you might imagine, because Caesarea just sort of means Caesar town."],[351.72,"So you could imagine in the Roman Empire there were a lot of towns named after him."],[358.92,"This is this is Caesarea Palestina."],[361.24,"This is Caesarea in Palestine."],[363.72,"It's how it's normally"],[370.04,"There's some debate about, because there are even a couple of towns called Caesarea."],[374.76,"s. It' usually this is the one near the Sea of Galilee"],[383.28,"And part of the issue with that when I say there's there's some debate is that one of the issues with identifying some of the towns around the Sea of Galilee is that the shore of the Sea of Galilee, where it is now, is very different from where it was in the first century."],[400.16,"So a lot of the towns that are described in the Gospels, for example, that are like coastal towns and fishing villages and that kind of thing are now like a mile away from the water, the remains"],[413.44,"And so that's made it harder for archaeologists and people working to kind of identify. for sure which one is which, because it's difficult to tell now because the landscape has sort of changed"],[427.32,"Yeah. Okay. So yeah, that's that's the generally agreed place."],[442.2,"That's um where this is."],[446.6,"And uh the uh the Italian regiment uh means that this is this is uh he's part of one of the legions that's actually from Rome."],[459.56,"There were at this point already."],[462.64,"Um keep in mind the Roman Empire. has really only has been around less than a hundred years at this point"],[469.28,"Um the ro Rome as a republic and everything, Rome as an entity, uh has been around for a lot longer."],[475.44,"But the Roman Empire is has been around for more limited amount of time."],[478.8,"But already at this point, uh the Roman military has started uh bringing in a lot of mercenaries because they've been, as you can imagine, you can't get enough soldiers from Italy to sort of guard and garrison and protect everywhere from Great Britain to Syria to North Africa."],[502.24,"Uh and so there are a lot of there are a lot of mercenaries who they've picked up."],[506.32,"There are a lot of uh people from those territories. who are serving in the military in order to earn their citizenship"],[513.96,"Because citizenship then wasn't like citizenship now, where it's based on where you were born, you had to earn it."],[521.08,"And very few people were actually Roman citizens."],[525.32,"But the only way to be born a Roman citizen is if your father was a Roman citizen, meaning he earned it, you know, sort of for himself and for his family."],[550.76,"And as a citizen, uh you would be given uh a certain piece of land, and usually that was out at the fringes of the empire."],[554.68,"of That's sort how the Romans did their expansion is that when a group of military veterans would sort of muster out, they'd give them a land grant sort of way out at the edge of their territory, and though they would go and build a new settlement there that would grow into a city."],[576.16,"Um but so the Italian regiment means that he's a native Roman."],[584.08,"He's from Italy."],[585.44,"That was then prestigious."],[588.3,"He's sort of a Roman of Romans."],[590.32,"He's not one of these mercenaries who had kind of worked his way up."],[593.52,"He's from sort of the upper class."],[596.0,"And as a centurion, the reason they were called centurions."],[601.61,"The word, yeah, you can see the word century in there, which means a hundred."],[606.81,"The the basic divisions of the Roman military were based on tens and hundreds."],[614.09,"So that a legion was made up of several centuries, groups of a hundred, and then a centurion was in command of each of those."],[625.13,"So they were sort of the smaller units, sort of the equivalent of a lieutenant or a captain."],[632.89,"Um in the modern military"],[633.73,"Yeah. But so this, and of course, uh your rank when you did muster out would determine sort of what kind of land grants and everything you would get."],[649.49,"So when he completed his career, since he was actually Italian, he would have been more in the track to end up becoming a governor somewhere, you know, or some other kind of official, you know, rather than just being given being given land the way an average enlisted uh person would."],[667.89,"So all this is to say not only is he a gentile and a Roman, but he is a high rank high rank in the military and has a high social status in terms of you know the the Roman community."],[685.25,"Um this also would have me meantant uh from a Jewish perspective."],[691.5,"He's not only a Gentile, but he's part of sort of the evil empire."],[698.0,"He's part of the oppressors who are here you know oppressing us."],[704.24,"However, we're gonna find out he's not like most centurions here in a second."],[708.8,"We're told in verse 2 a devout man and one who feared God with all his household, who gave alms generously to the people and prayed to God always."],[720.64,"So we need to be clear here."],[723.64,"When this is being written by Saint Luke, this doesn't mean he's devout like he's really faithful to Zeus."],[730.96,"It goes to the pagan temples a lot."],[734.1,"But it says he's a devout man who feared God."],[737.44,"This is God in the singular."],[740.4,"It means he's a he's someone who fears the God of Israel."],[745.52,"And this phrase, a God fearer, was a little bit of a technical term at this time in history."],[754.32,"Because there was a great, I mentioned this before, I know, but there was a great fascination by the Romans in Judaism for a couple of reasons."],[766.24,"Number one, it was very ancient."],[769.01,"And anything very ancient, they were sort of intrigued by."],[771.73,"Same thing held with the Egyptians, sort of Egyptian mythology of the Egyptians they thought was really interesting because it was so old."],[776.45,"It was older than their civilization"],[781.29,"So they were intrigued with it on that level, but even more so because Judaism was from their perspective so weird."],[790.17,"Weird in that they only had this one god."],[793.31,"And they only had this one temple in one place, where of course they had all kinds of gods and all kinds of temples."],[807.31,"So it was odd in that way."],[809.15,"And then the event that sort of really touched this off was that at the time when uh General Pompeii uh in uh the first century BC, it was around 63, came to annex Judea."],[820.99,"Judea had been sort of semi-independent"],[827.75,"They'd had a peace treaty with the Romans, and then the Romans sort of turned that treaty into, well, you're part of us now."],[834.55,"Annexed Judea. Uh and when uh Pompeii the General came with his army to announce that to everybody and brought an army with him just in case anybody had a problem with that."],[846.15,"Um he also insisted on going into the temple, which of course they didn't want him to do because he was a Gentile."],[855.13,"And he wanted not only wanted to go into the temple, he wanted to go all the way into the temple."],[859.93,"And he ended up actually going into the Holy of Holies in the temple."],[865.09,"But when he went there and he went back behind the veil there was nothing there"],[865.5,"Which no one's allowed to except the hybrid."],[872.62,"Which really confused him."],[874.46,"Because he was expecting to see some kind of idol there or some kind of treasure or some kind of something."],[881.74,"Because he said there's got to be something back in there behind this curtain that they don't let anyone see, and I want to see what it is."],[887.02,"And he went back there and there wasn't anything there."],[890.22,"So what he decided was he decided that Judaism must be this great religion."],[896.14,"Because he said they worship their gods sola mentis, only with their mind."],[902.31,"And so, sort of the philosophically minded Greeks and Romans picked up on this and said, Oh, you know, this is. you know, yeah, we're going around killing these animals and using statues and all this"],[914.51,"Yeah, that's this is a higher sophisticated."],[918.32,"Yeah, this is this is this higher philosophical form of religion."],[921.44,"So this got a lot of Greeks and Romans sort of fascinated with Judaism and interested in Judaism."],[928.96,"Um sort of the way a whole bunch of celebrities got into Kabbalah about 10 years ago."],[934.24,"I don't know."],[935.76,"That was like the in thing, a bunch of celebrities."],[938.64,"But so they got fascinated by now, they weren't fascinated enough that they were gonna go and get circumcised and stop eating pork and you know, go and do all this stuff to actually become Jewish."],[950.56,"They weren't that interested."],[952.3,"That they were gonna convert."],[953.42,"Uh but they were interested"],[957.14,"And so we found in in archaeological excavations of these first century synagogues, especially in Roman towns, uh, there'll be sort of a dedication stone that'll list the names of all the donors, who helped build the synagogue."],[975.16,"And a large number of the names are not Jewish names."],[980.1,"They're Roman and Greek names."],[982.18,"Because these people who are sort of fascinated by Judaism, they would give money to the synagogue."],[989.32,"As a way of sort of showing benefaction."],[992.12,"And hey, you know, maybe, you know, if they're God, you know, we'll take that into account and help me out, you know, sometime later when I need it."],[997.32,"You know Um so that and those people, who were who were who did that were referred to as God fearers."],[1009.89,"They were people who showed this reverence toward the God of Israel, but they weren't c converts."],[1017.33,"They weren't actually Jews."],[1019.89,"But they had, yeah, they had some kind of reverence for for Israel's God."],[1024.61,"And so this is saying that Cornelius is one of those people."],[1028.95,"Cornelius is one of those people."],[1031.67,"And when it says that he gave generously to the people, the people means the Jews."],[1038.47,"Not just to everybody who was in need, but it means. he was giving money to the Jewish community to help support it"],[1046.83,"Okay. And he prayed to God always."],[1052.35,"That's important. The always is important."],[1055.07,"Because it doesn't just mean he prayed all the time."],[1057.71,"It means he only prayed to Israel's God."],[1062.83,"Because some of those God fearers would just sort of add him to the list."],[1072.83,"Oh, yeah, we'll add one more at the end."],[1074.59,"Israel's God, because he seems kind of interesting too, and it can't hurt to cover cover all your bases."],[1080.37,"The ancient Roman warrior uh Roman campaigning armies actually h.eld sacrifices to the native gods of a landing"],[1092.97,"To win a demigod."],[1094.66,"To try and w win the mobile."],[1096.02,"And these statues of these people, and guess what?"],[1098.1,"They weren't even gods."],[1099.22,"They weren't nothing."],[1100.58,"It was just a statue."],[1102.98,"So they didn't they didn't feel like you always had to pick one, just one."],[1107.06,"But we're being told that Cornelius, it was just the God of Israel."],[1111.94,"That was the only God who he who he was praying to."],[1118.66,"And so this is this is going to be important because uh most of we're gonna read as we go through the rest of the book of Acts, especially when St."],[1128.02,"Paul goes off on his missionary jour.neys about a lot of Gentiles converting to Christianity, Gentiles becoming Christians"],[1137.02,"And almost all of those Gentiles are going to come from these God fearers."],[1143.58,"And the reason that's important is what we're going to see is that when St."],[1146.86,"Paul goes to these towns and these people start becoming Christians, the Jews in that town are going to get very upset."],[1155.8,"The Jewish community."],[1160.16,"Do they care?"],[1161.86,"Why do they care if this pagan is worshiping Jesus instead of Zeus?"],[1169.32,"I mean, yeah, Jews don't believe in Jesus, they also don't believe in Zeus."],[1173.8,"So, you know, why does it matter to them?"],[1175.8,"Well, the reason it matters to them is once these people become Christians, they start giving their money to the Christian community instead of the Jewish community."],[1185.42,"They start supporting the Christians instead of supporting the local synagogue."],[1191.42,"And so the the money and the social influence and all that that these Jewish communities had in these cities starts to disappear when St."],[1201.18,"Paul starts stealing their God fear fearers."],[1205.66,"And so this cause is what causes them to get very, very angry at St."],[1209.74,"Paul, as we'll see later."],[1212.54,"When they join Christianity, they become believers."],[1216.06,"They are not joining Christianity because of the fear of God."],[1219.74,"And this is different."],[1221.2,"And and this is, we're going to see in a few chapters, this is going to become a big issue in the church too, because there's going to be this question well, if these people, because right now, pretty much all of the Christians are Jews."],[1241.11,"Meaning they were all circumcised and they all did everything."],[1244.63,"You know, the Old Testament, they're keeping all the food rules and everything."],[1247.59,"Well, when these God fearers, when they become Christians, do they need to do all that stuff too?"],[1254.49,"Do they need to sort of become Jews first?"],[1256.65,"But that's going to become an issue."],[1259.13,"And so the answer is ultimately going to be if with most of that, no, they don't need to do it."],[1265.73,"Which is also going to be another issue, in terms of the Jewish community."],[1271.04,"Because the way they're going to see that is, oh, look, you know, these people want to want to worship the God of Israel, but won't commit to doing all these things."],[1281.04,"And so then St."],[1281.84,"Paul shows up and says, Oh, you don't have to do any of that to join my group."],[1286.22,"And so that's part of the right."],[1288.7,"And that's why they start making these accusations against St."],[1291.42,"Paul. Well, you're just trying to toss the law out the window."],[1295.68,"You're just trying to destroy all the traditions of our people, you know, by not having them do these things."],[1302.64,"Most of them they they made these laws."],[1304.24,"But some of them, I mean, circumcision is in the old testament"],[1305.16,"It's not a lot of them, yeah."],[1307.08,"Yeah, most of the people."],[1310.92,"I mean, so yeah, yeah."],[1315.32,"All the all of those that there are a lot of those things that are in the old testament."],[1318.76,"And there are some that they've added."],[1320.6,"Yeah. That's um some more that they've added."],[1324.04,"So but so Cornelius is sort of our first one of these God fears who we're meeting."],[1331.08,"Okay. So even though he he he's an interesting person in that he is both sort of represents the enemy of the Jewish people, in that he's this high-ranking, high social status Roman military person, on the other hand, he's a very pious person. and has done everything but convert"],[1352.4,"He's only and so then notice in in verse 3 about the ninth hour of the day, he saw clearly in a vision an angel of God coming in and saying to him, Cornelius."],[1366.56,"Now, why is it important that it's the ninth hour of the day?"],[1368.88,"Well, that's one of the hours of prayer for the Jewish people."],[1372.56,"We saw, remember, earlier in the book of Acts, the apostles at one point were going to the temple at the ninth hour to pray."],[1379.12,"So he's even praying at the time."],[1383.44,"So he's keeping some of those, at least some of those traditions."],[1388.56,"And so as he's praying, he has this vision of this angel of God coming in who, says to him, Cornelius."],[1394.24,"So he said to him Your prayers and your alms have come up for a memorial before God."],[1395.8,"And when he observed him, he was afraid and said, What is it, Lord?"],[1410.6,"So two pieces with that."],[1412.52,"First, he says, Your prayers and your alms giving have come up at a memorial for God, meaning God's noticed."],[1420.25,"Your prayers and the the alms you get meaning what you've given to the poor, what you've given to those who are in need."],[1427.77,"But the word the word memorial there is important"],[1434.25,"Because uh memorial, if you think about it, well the way we use memorial is what?"],[1441.09,"Remembrance of the dead."],[1442.05,"Remember it remembrance of something, but yeah, often the dead, but the yeah."],[1446.69,"Um whereas that's clearly not what this is talking about."],[1453.22,"That's it's not that God remembered something because."],[1457.04,"In the sense that we think about remembering the past."],[1459.98,"The word the word that's translated memorial in Greek uh means something more like having something in mind."],[1469.48,"It's not remember like I remember three years ago when such and such happened."],[1475.56,"It's more like uh I remembered to feed the dog."],[1480.53,"I remembered to lock my car."],[1483.02,"It was in my mind."],[1483.98,"It didn't slip my mind."],[1485.68,"It was it was in my mind."],[1488.24,"And so when we talk about something being a memorial for God."],[1492.66,"We don't mean like God forgets what's going on and oh you reminded me, thanks."],[1498.24,"You know, but we we mean that God has it in mind."],[1502.1,"This is why we we sing memory eternal when we're talking about those who are departed, because if God remembers this person, if God has them in mind forever, then they exist forever."],[1516.58,"Memorial is also used, for example, in Numbers 10 10 in the Greek, that same word. is used for sacrifices, for sin offerings"],[1530.66,"And so it has this meaning of an offering, an offering to God."],[1538.9,"And this is what it's translated."],[1540.58,"That brings you to mind."],[1541.56,"Is it uh sat like a sacrifice?"],[1543.24,"Yeah, this is what it's translated."],[1545.88,"Um, and so uh the reason I'm making such a point of this is that famously, uh Christ says at the Last Supper, when he says, This is my body broken for you for remission of sins, this is my blood shed for you, my blood of the new covenant shed for you for remission of sins."],[1566.36,"He says, sa Doys Do this as literally, it this as my memorial."],[1572.34,"And so some of our Protestant friends read that and think, Oh, well, this means we remember Jesus."],[1578.76,"While we do it, but that's not how that word is used in the scriptures."],[1584.06,"When Jesus says, This is my memorial, he's saying, This is my offering."],[1589.67,"This is this is my sacrifice, and so he's talking about um the Eucharist."],[1597.45,"Communion, as we celebrate it, taking the place of the sacrifices in the Old Testament."],[1602.41,"We don't do those anymore."],[1604.19,"Now we celebrate the Eucharist and participate in Christ's sacrifice."],[1609.51,"And so what the angel is really saying to Cornelius is that these things you've been doing, the prayers you've been offering to God, you know, the way you've been helping the poor, God has received this as a sacrifice from you."],[1626.47,"He's received this as an offering from you."],[1631.99,"And this is right when we when we well, tonight it was read, but when we read or sing."],[1641.92,"Let my prayers are prayer rise in your sight as incense and the lifting up of my hands be an evening sacrifice."],[1649.28,"We're talking about the same kind of thing that God would receive our prayers as a sacrifice and as an offering, the way he received Cornelius's."],[1679.68,"Tanner is someone who works with leather."],[1683.2,"In Joppa on the coast."],[1686.52,"And so the angel tells him, go send somebody to get this guy and do what he tells you."],[1697.4,"And when the angel who spoke to him had departed, Cornelius called two of his household servants and a devout soldier from among those who waited on him continually."],[1709.0,"So when he explained all these things to them, he sent them to Joppa."],[1714.36,"So he then sends them to go and uh to go and get um Saint Peter."],[1724.76,"One other interesting note here, and that's um a lot of times, one of the questions I as a priest, and one of the questions that I think Christians in general get asked a lot is uh what happens to people who live their whole life and die and never hear about Jesus."],[1745.3,"Who never know anything about Jesus?"],[1747.94,"Well, this is the this is the one passage where we see something of that."],[1753.47,"Because Cornelius not only didn't know about Jesus, he had no real way of finding out the time and place, the time and place he was living."],[1761.87,"But what he did know, what he had learned, what he had been taught, he was faithful to that and followed God as best he knew how."],[1772.69,"And so God arranges for him, okay in this case through sort of supernatural means, but God arranges for him to find out more."],[1785.93,"And so while we as human beings, we aren't the ones who judge, so we can't ever say, oh, this person is good and this person is bad, and you know where people will end up before the judgment seat of Christ on the last day."],[1802.33,"This tells us that people, every human being who has lived in this world has known something about God by virtue of being made in his image, by virtue of living in his world, in his creation, by being able to look around and see what he's created."],[1823.61,"And so uh what we can see in principle here, at the beginning of chapter 10, is that if if people are faithful with what they receive, that God honors that, he receives that, as a sacrifice and offering to himself, and that he will give them more in order that they'll have what they need."],[1847.68,"So at the end of time, God will ask you about the things that you know and that you learned, and that's how we will be judged."],[1858.24,"So by what we did with what he gave us."],[1860.56,"What he gave us, yes."],[1861.92,"So the more we know, the more we will be responsible to keep what we know."],[1867.3,"As long as you don't know, you don't know."],[1869.14,"But when you know, you have to be responsible because you received the words."],[1873.54,"And I try not to spell that out because then everyone stopped showing up for Bible study because they don't want to know anymore."],[1885.87,"But and that and that's what Christ says over and over again."],[1888.81,"From him who has been given much, much will be required."],[1892.97,"And this we're gonna see Saint Paul sort of echo this at the beginning of his epistle to the Romans, where he's going to talk about uh specifically to the Jewish people and say, you know, look, you received you know the Torah, you received all these risks, all these things."],[1909.61,"That makes you more accountable than these Gentiles who didn't receive any of that."],[1914.17,"And then he's gonna say, but at the same time, some of these Gentiles who didn't receive any of that have done a better job. of living a moral life and keeping the laws of God than you have, even though they didn't know them"],[1926.85,"Just based on their own conscience and on you know living in the world."],[1932.21,"So yeah, that's that's the principle."],[1935.09,"And so the answer to when that question comes is twofold."],[1940.69,"Number one, we need to spend more time looking at our own paper and not at other people's papers."],[1945.97,"You know, and not what not worrying about them, worrying about ourselves and and what we're doing with what God has given us."],[1953.09,"Um but also that that that is the truth, that God holds people accountable for what they do with what He's given them."],[1961.49,"And God gives different people different blessings."],[1963.01,"blessings. And what you do with those is what's important, not how many of them you receive"],[1971.45,"And comparing that to other people."],[1977.69,"So he has now sent off one of his soldiers and a couple of his servants to go find this Simon Peter fellow down in Joppa, which is quite the journey from Caesarea."],[1990.33,"So there's going to be some time involved here."],[1993.53,"The next day, as they went on their journey and drew near the city, Peter went up on the housetop to pray about the sixth hour."],[2001.21,"Okay, so it's the sixth hour, and Saint Peter likewise is going to pray his prayers."],[2008.65,"Then he became very hungry and wanted to eat."],[2009.93,"Okay But while they made ready, he fell into a trance."],[2016.77,"So he's very hungry."],[2017.97,"Sixth hour is about noon."],[2019.91,"So this is lunch."],[2021.21,"So he's very hungry."],[2022.73,"They're cooking lunch downstairs while he's saying his prayers."],[2027.37,"And uh, but while they're while they're getting the food ready, he falls into a falls into a trance, is how they translate the Orthodox Study Bible."],[2035.53,"The idea is basically he has a vision now, sort of in the same way that Cornelius had had a had had a vision while he's praying."],[2044.41,"And he saw heaven opened and an object like a great sheet bound at the four corners, descending to him and let down to the earth."],[2053.05,"Okay, so he sees this big thing, it looks like an upside-down parachute."],[2053.77,"es this. It's got rop of the four corners, big sheet"],[2060.69,"It's coming out of the sky."],[2064.23,"Coming down from heaven."],[2067.03,"It's a little odd, but it's not the weirdest vision in the Bible."],[2069.67,"Go back to Ezekiel and you'll see some really wild stuff."],[2075.11,"In it were all kinds of four-footed animals of the earth, wild beasts, creeping things, and birds of the air."],[2081.35,"The creeping things there is basically insects."],[2085.91,"Some of the four-footed animals were there."],[2087.71,"The word one of the words there is is Herpetone, which means reptiles."],[2091.75,"I know we're in Louisiana, so none of this sounds as gross as it would in other places."],[2097.83,"Eat some rept.ile all the time"],[2107.84,"So they've got the very strict food laws."],[2110.48,"Yeah. Okay. So this voice says, Hey, you're hungry."],[2121.3,"Have at it."],[2122.82,"Here are all these animals."],[2125.2,"And and the the idea of eating the animals is not the only important thing."],[2129.04,"Notice it says kill and eat."],[2131.3,"Meaning he's also not going to be able to follow a lot of the food laws were about how you prepare the food."],[2138.56,"How you killed the animals, draining the blood, preparing it."],[2141.64,"The correct way to do that in order to be allowed to eat it."],[2144.76,"So not only is he being told to eat these things he's not supposed to eat, he's being basically told to kill them and eat them raw."],[2152.36,"Oh no. I haven't tried that before."],[2157.56,"So this is not appetizing."],[2161.33,"As hungry as he is, this is not an appetizing proposition."],[2165.41,"And uh it goes against his whole cultural upbringing."],[2170.69,"It goes against So is that because he's saying that the pot is coming from heaven, it's upside down, and he sees the animals inside."],[2178.13,"The animals are in it."],[2179.17,"Yes, so the enemies."],[2180.53,"It's like an upside an upside down, no, it's like an upside down parachute."],[2183.65,"Yeah, okay. Where it's like this."],[2185.51,"And when it comes low enough, he can see that it's full of it's like a big sheet."],[2190.52,"I was always confused about what seed."],[2192.68,"Yeah. And when it comes down far enough, he can see that it's full of all these animals."],[2197.34,"That's what's right, these unclean animals."],[2199.58,"And then he gets told get up and kill some of these and and have lunch."],[2209.74,"But Peter said, not so, Lord, for I've never eaten anything common or unclean."],[2215.28,"So he says, Oh, no, no, no, no, no."],[2217.36,"This is clearly this is a test."],[2221.2,"Because I would never eat anything like that."],[2224.72,"I never have."],[2226.08,"I would never do that."],[2227.84,"And a voice spoke to him again the second time what God is cleansed, you must not call common"],[2235.88,"That's not the best translation."],[2238.28,"It's basically what God has made clean, do not call unclean."],[2244.36,"This was done three times, and the object was taken up into heaven again."],[2250.28,"Now notice this was done three times because apparently each time St."],[2255.16,"Peter said, uh uh."],[2260.84,"He said, no."],[2263.28,"But notice, notice what is said to him."],[2266.74,"Notice what it said, because it's important how this is worded."],[2270.12,"What's said to him isn't, oh, that's a silly superstition, it's okay to eat this stuff."],[2271.4,"'t. They don say that"],[2278.13,"Right? They don't say, oh, you're that's not what that's not what the Torah says."],[2283.51,"It's okay to eat this."],[2284.55,"Or don't worry about how you kill animals."],[2287.59,"Just go ahead and eat things."],[2289.28,"It's none of that."],[2290.24,"What is said is when you call these things unclean, you're calling something that God has made clean."],[2298.24,"Meaning it wasn't always clean."],[2300.8,"But it is now."],[2303.84,"And since God has now made it clean, you need to not be calling it unclean."],[2311.6,"So he's like he's giving him the permission to start eating of this stuff."],[2314.8,"It's not permission"],[2316.44,"Well, it's it's not it's not permission."],[2319.96,"It's that uh it's it's God is saying to St."],[2323.4,"Peter that something has changed."],[2326.04,"Oh, that's fine."],[2327.32,"That something has changed."],[2328.68,"It's not that the rule doesn't apply anymore."],[2331.96,"Oh, okay. We're still supposed to, we're gonna see later in St."],[2335.02,"Paul's epistles, he's gonna quote Leviticus and say, touch no unclean thing."],[2339.58,"Stay away from unclean things."],[2341.66,"Okay, so it's still wrong."],[2345.16,"To to be unclean and to deal with unclean things, but something has changed in terms of what is and isn't unclean."],[2353.88,"So that was the message?"],[2355.88,"That that is the message."],[2357.24,"Now it's saying that right now about animals."],[2362.33,"Because in the Old Testament, you have clean animals and unclean animals."],[2367.78,"And by and large, by and large, without going into huge amounts of detail."],[2373.94,"We can go into huge amounts of detail, like in Leviticus, where like the owl and the nighthawk and the sparrow are unclean birds and all that."],[2380.82,"But it in general, the animals that are clean are animals that are domesticated and are kept in the camp and raised for food."],[2390.66,"And the animals that are unclean are wild animals and scavengers and right that live outside the camp in the world."],[2399.78,"Because what we see in the Old Testament, especially in the Torah, especially in Leviticus, that has a lot of these rules, is that there's this distinction made between the camp, which is where Israel lives, which is where God lives with them in the tabernacle."],[2414.46,"This area that is clean and that they have to keep clean because God lives there."],[2419.66,"Remember, we talked about this with Ananias and Sapphira."],[2422.54,"The people coming into the presence of God who are wicked is dangerous."],[2431.26,"And by and by keeping it clean."],[2433.82,"And then the rest of the world is unclean."],[2437.98,"Yeah. Rest of the world is unclean."],[2440.19,"And we saw this in the Gospels, like in the Gospel of John, you know, of St."],[2444.35,"John, when we were going through, where Jesus refers to Satan as the prince of this world."],[2449.37,"The rest of the world out there that's under under sin that's under the power of the devil."],[2455.26,"Well, something has changed."],[2459.31,"Because Christ has been crucified and has risen from the dead."],[2464.85,"And when he did that, what did he do?"],[2467.57,"Well, he defeated death, he defeated sin, defeated hell, he defeated Satan."],[2474.33,"So who's ruling over the whole world now?"],[2479.21,"Jesus. The whole world, not just the camp, not just Jerusalem, not just the Jewish people."],[2488.15,"The whole world."],[2489.67,"The whole world belongs to him now."],[2492.47,"Okay. That includes all the animals."],[2497.93,"There's no outside of his kingdom anymore."],[2501.85,"In terms of his creation."],[2505.23,"So this means the whole material world, the whole material creation is clean now."],[2511.55,"Okay. That's what we see in the vision."],[2515.07,"Now, why would God send Saint Peter this vision right now?"],[2521.23,"Who's on their way to talk to him?"],[2525.39,"A bunch of Gentiles."],[2528.11,"To invite him to do what?"],[2530.27,"To come as a Jewish person. into a Gentile's house"],[2535.35,"And not just a Gentile, a Roman."],[2538.09,"A really Gentile Gentile."],[2541.45,"As Gentiles you get."],[2542.81,"And Gentiles are what, as far as the Jews are concerned?"],[2546.33,"Of Satan. Unclean."],[2548.17,"Unclean. They're unclean."],[2551.05,"They're one of those other peoples."],[2553.53,"Not the Jewish people."],[2556.81,"And so he's."],[2558.49,"This vision uses the example of animals."],[2561.85,"But it's really talking about the whole world and the whole creation."],[2565.29,"Because just as no animal and no part of the world now isn't under the rule of Christ, now that he's ascended into heaven and is enthroned."],[2573.42,"This ruling over the world, but there's no person, there's no people out there who are outside of Christ's reign."],[2583.78,"They may not be loyal subjects."],[2585.8,"But he's still their Lord, whether they like it or not."],[2589.96,"So he's ruling over everyone."],[2592.44,"And that means no person is unclean."],[2597.16,"So he uses this object lesson of telling him to do something horribly unclean to kill these animals and eat them raw."],[2606.12,"To make the point that you're about to be asked to do something else that you're gonna think is unclean, is bad, is something you shouldn't do, is something you need to stay separate from."],[2617.0,"But since God has made this man Cornelius clean. clean, don't you dare go andall him unc"],[2627.66,"Or filthy. Listen next time as Father Stephen DeYoung continues his study of the scriptures on the whole counsel of God."],[2638.94,"Father Stephen's email address is wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."],[2644.3,"That's wholecounsel at ancientfaith.com."]],"o":[{"t":21.04,"lv":2,"h":"Recap: where Acts stands","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Picking up <b>Acts 10:1</b>; first Bible study on Acts (intro) available to listen to</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Acts 1</b>: Ascension; <b>witnesses in Jerusalem, Judea, Samaria, ends of the earth</b></li><li class=\"d1\">that's the <b>plan unfolding</b> as we go</li><li class=\"d0\">Early chapters all in <b>Jerusalem</b> itself</li><li class=\"d1\">growing, but not beyond it - except visitors who heard and <b>took it home</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Stephen</b> stoned by chief priests and rulers -> <b>persecution scattered</b> people</li><li class=\"d1\">intent: <b>get rid of Christians</b>; result: <b>spread Christianity over the countryside</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Philip</b> preached in <b>Samaria</b>, baptized the <b>Ethiopian eunuch</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Acts 9</b>: <b>Saul</b> at Stephen's execution, <b>road to Damascus</b>; <b>Ananias</b> baptized him, sight back</li><li class=\"d1\">fled Damascus - <b>let down through the wall</b>; Jerusalem unsure, <b>Barnabas</b> vouched</li></ul>"},{"t":252.44,"lv":3,"h":"Peter on the move","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">End of ch. 9: <b>Peter</b> out of Jerusalem into <b>Judea</b>, village to village</li><li class=\"d0\">Luke's start: gospel = all Jesus <b>began to do and teach</b> -> apostles <b>continue</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Peter <b>healing the sick</b>, <b>raising a dead girl</b> (Tabitha)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>preaching the kingdom of God</b> as Jesus did</li><li class=\"d0\">Picking up with Peter at ch. 10</li></ul>"},{"t":335.88,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 10:1 - Cornelius the centurion","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Cornelius</b>, centurion of the <b>Italian regiment</b>, in <b>Caesarea</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Caesarea</b> = \"Caesar town\" - many in the Empire</li><li class=\"d1\">this = <b>Caesarea Palestina</b>, in Palestine</li><li class=\"d1\">debate over towns by <b>Sea of Galilee</b> - shoreline in 1st c. very different</li><li class=\"d1\">coastal towns now <b>a mile from the water</b> - hard for archaeologists</li><li class=\"d1\">generally agreed place</li></ul>"},{"t":446.6,"lv":3,"h":"Italian regiment and Roman citizenship","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Italian regiment = a <b>legion actually from Rome</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Empire <b>less than 100 years old</b>; Rome as republic much older</li><li class=\"d1\">military already bringing in <b>mercenaries</b> - can't staff Britain to Syria to N. Africa from Italy</li><li class=\"d1\">they serve <b>to earn citizenship</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Citizenship</b> then = <b>earned</b>, not by birthplace</li><li class=\"d1\">born citizen only if <b>father</b> was one</li><li class=\"d1\">citizens given <b>land grants</b> at the <b>fringes</b> of the empire</li><li class=\"d1\">veterans' settlements grow into <b>cities</b> - how Romans expanded</li><li class=\"d0\">Italian regiment = <b>native Roman</b>, <b>\"Roman of Romans\"</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not a mercenary who worked his way up - <b>upper class</b></li></ul>"},{"t":596.0,"lv":3,"h":"Centurion: rank and status","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Century</b> = hundred; military built on <b>tens and hundreds</b></li><li class=\"d1\">legion = several centuries; <b>centurion</b> commands each</li><li class=\"d1\">~ <b>lieutenant or captain</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Rank at muster-out decides land grants</li><li class=\"d1\">an Italian = track toward <b>governor or official</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Gentile, Roman, <b>high rank, high social status</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Jewish view</b>: Gentile + part of the <b>\"evil empire\"</b>, <b>oppressors</b></li><li class=\"d1\">but \"<b>not like most centurions</b>\"</li></ul>"},{"t":708.8,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 10:2 - A God-fearer","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Devout</b>, <b>feared God</b> with all his household, gave <b>alms generously</b>, <b>prayed always</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not devout to <b>Zeus</b>, going to pagan temples</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>God in the singular</b> = <b>God of Israel</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>\"God-fearer\"</b> = a <b>technical term</b> then</li><li class=\"d0\">Roman <b>fascination with Judaism</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>very ancient</b> - like Egyptian mythology older than their civilization</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>weird</b>: <b>one god, one temple</b> in one place - they had many gods, many temples</li></ul>"},{"t":809.15,"lv":3,"h":"Pompey in the Holy of Holies","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Pompey</b>, ~<b>63 BC</b>, annexed <b>Judea</b></li><li class=\"d1\">semi-independent, peace treaty -> \"you're part of us now\"</li><li class=\"d1\">came with an <b>army</b> in case of objections</li><li class=\"d0\">Insisted on entering the <b>temple</b>, then the <b>Holy of Holies</b></li><li class=\"d1\">behind the veil: <b>nothing there</b> - expected idol or treasure</li><li class=\"d1\">concluded: great religion - worship \"<b>with the mind only</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Philosophical Greeks and Romans: <b>higher, sophisticated religion</b></li><li class=\"d1\">like celebrities into <b>Kabbalah</b> ~10 years ago</li><li class=\"d1\">not enough to <b>circumcise, stop eating pork, convert</b></li></ul>"},{"t":957.14,"lv":3,"h":"Gentile donors and God-fearers","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">1st-c. <b>synagogue dedication stones</b> list donors</li><li class=\"d1\">many <b>Roman and Greek names</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>benefaction</b> - \"maybe their God will help me sometime\"</li><li class=\"d0\">These = <b>God-fearers</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>reverence</b> for Israel's God, <b>not converts</b>, not Jews</li><li class=\"d0\">Cornelius is one</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>\"the people\"</b> = the <b>Jews</b> - supporting the <b>Jewish community</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>\"always\"</b> = prayed <b>only</b> to Israel's God</li><li class=\"d1\">some God-fearers just <b>added Him to the list</b> - \"can't hurt to cover all your bases\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Roman armies sacrificed to the <b>native gods</b> of a land they invaded - didn't feel you had to pick one</li><li class=\"d1\">Cornelius: <b>only the God of Israel</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1118.66,"lv":2,"h":"Why God-fearers matter for Acts","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Rest of Acts, <b>Paul's missionary journeys</b>: Gentile converts</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>almost all from God-fearers</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Jews in town get <b>very upset</b> - why care if a pagan worships Jesus not Zeus?</li><li class=\"d1\">converts give <b>money to the Christian community</b>, not the <b>synagogue</b></li><li class=\"d1\">loss of <b>money and social influence</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Paul is \"<b>stealing their God-fearers</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">They join Christianity as <b>believers</b>, not out of fear of God</li></ul>"},{"t":1219.74,"lv":3,"h":"Do Gentiles have to become Jews first?","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Now nearly all Christians are <b>Jews</b> - circumcised, keeping <b>food rules</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Do God-fearers who become Christians have to <b>become Jews first</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>big issue</b> in a few chapters</li><li class=\"d1\">answer: <b>no</b>, for most of it</li><li class=\"d0\">Jewish view: \"want to worship Israel's God, <b>won't commit</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Paul: \"you don't have to do any of that to join\"</li><li class=\"d1\">accusations: <b>throwing the law out</b>, <b>destroying traditions</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Q: some of it in OT - <b>circumcision</b>; others <b>added later</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Cornelius = first God-fearer</b> we meet</li><li class=\"d1\">enemy (<b>high-ranking Roman</b>) yet <b>very pious</b>, everything <b>but convert</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1352.4,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 10:3-4 - The angel's vision","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Ninth hour</b> - one of the <b>Jewish hours of prayer</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Acts: apostles went to temple at the ninth hour</li><li class=\"d1\">Cornelius keeping <b>some of those traditions</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Angel of God</b>: \"<b>Cornelius</b>\"; afraid: \"What is it, Lord?\"</li><li class=\"d0\">\"<b>Your prayers and alms have come up for a memorial before God</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>God has noticed</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1427.77,"lv":3,"h":"\"Memorial\" means having in mind","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">English \"memorial\" = <b>remembrance of the dead</b></li><li class=\"d1\">Greek: <b>having something in mind</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not \"remember 3 years ago\" - \"<b>I remembered to feed the dog</b>\", lock my car</li><li class=\"d1\">not God forgetting - <b>God has it in mind</b></li><li class=\"d1\">why we sing <b>\"memory eternal\"</b> - if God keeps them in mind forever, they <b>exist forever</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Same word in <b>Numbers 10:10</b> (Greek) for <b>sacrifices, sin offerings</b></li><li class=\"d1\">= <b>an offering to God</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1545.88,"lv":3,"h":"Memorial at the Last Supper","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Last Supper: \"this is my body... blood of the new covenant for remission of sins\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"Do this as <b>my memorial</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Protestant reading: <b>we remember Jesus</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not how the word works in Scripture = \"<b>this is my offering, my sacrifice</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Eucharist</b> replaces OT sacrifices - <b>participate in Christ's sacrifice</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Angel to Cornelius: prayers and almsgiving <b>received as a sacrifice, an offering</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>Let my prayer rise as incense</b>, lifting of my hands an <b>evening sacrifice</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">God receives our prayers as sacrifice, as he did Cornelius's</li></ul>"},{"t":1679.68,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 10:5-8 - Send for Peter","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\"><b>Tanner</b> = works with <b>leather</b>; in <b>Joppa</b> on the coast</li><li class=\"d0\">Angel: \"send somebody to get this guy and <b>do what he tells you</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">Cornelius called <b>two household servants</b> and a <b>devout soldier</b> who waited on him</li><li class=\"d1\">explained everything, <b>sent them to Joppa</b> for <b>Peter</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1724.76,"lv":2,"h":"Those who never hear of Jesus","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Common question: <b>what happens to people who never hear about Jesus</b>?</li><li class=\"d1\">this is the <b>one passage</b> where we see something of it</li><li class=\"d0\">Cornelius: <b>no real way of finding out</b></li><li class=\"d1\">was <b>faithful to what he knew</b>, followed God as best he could</li><li class=\"d1\">God <b>arranges for him to find out more</b> - here by supernatural means</li><li class=\"d0\">We <b>aren't the ones who judge</b> - can't say who ends up where</li><li class=\"d0\">Every human knows something of God: <b>made in his image</b>, <b>creation</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>faithful with what they receive</b> -> God receives it as <b>sacrifice and offering</b>, gives more</li><li class=\"d1\">judged by <b>what we did with what he gave us</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>the more we know, the more responsible</b> - \"as long as you don't know, you don't know\"</li><li class=\"d1\">joke: don't spell it out or <b>no one shows up to Bible study</b></li></ul>"},{"t":1885.87,"lv":3,"h":"Echo in Romans; the twofold answer","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Christ: \"<b>From him who has been given much, much will be required</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Romans</b> opening: Jews got the <b>Torah</b> -> <b>more accountable</b> than Gentiles</li><li class=\"d1\">yet some Gentiles lived <b>more morally</b> by <b>conscience</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Answer is <b>twofold</b></li><li class=\"d1\">look at <b>our own paper</b>, not other people's</li><li class=\"d1\">God holds people accountable for <b>what they do with what He's given</b></li><li class=\"d1\">different people get <b>different blessings</b>; what matters = <b>what you do with them</b>, not how many, not comparison</li></ul>"},{"t":1977.69,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 10:9-12 - Peter's trance","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Soldier and servants sent to Joppa - <b>quite a journey</b> from Caesarea, takes time</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Next day</b>: Peter on the <b>housetop</b> to pray, <b>sixth hour</b> (~<b>noon</b>)</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>very hungry</b>; lunch cooking downstairs</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Trance</b> (Orthodox Study Bible) = a <b>vision</b>, like Cornelius's</li><li class=\"d0\">Saw <b>heaven opened</b>, object like a <b>great sheet bound at four corners</b>, let down to earth</li><li class=\"d1\">\"upside-down parachute\"</li><li class=\"d1\">not the weirdest vision - \"go back to <b>Ezekiel</b>\"</li><li class=\"d0\">In it: <b>four-footed animals, wild beasts, creeping things</b> (insects), <b>birds</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b><i>herpeton</i></b> = reptiles - joke: Louisiana, \"eat reptile all the time\"</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>strict food laws</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2110.48,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 10:13-14 - Kill and eat","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Voice: \"<b>Rise, Peter; kill and eat</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"<b>kill</b>\" matters - food laws also about <b>preparation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">how you kill, <b>draining the blood</b></li><li class=\"d1\">told to eat unclean animals <b>and kill and eat them raw</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Not appetizing</b> however hungry; <b>against his whole upbringing</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Peter: \"<b>Not so, Lord</b>, I've never eaten anything <b>common or unclean</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">\"clearly a <b>test</b>\" - \"I never have, I never would\"</li></ul>"},{"t":2227.84,"lv":2,"h":"Acts 10:15-16 - What God has cleansed","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Voice again: \"<b>What God has cleansed, do not call common</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">better: <b>what God has made clean, do not call unclean</b></li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Done three times</b>; object taken up to heaven</li><li class=\"d1\">three times because Peter said <b>no</b> each time</li><li class=\"d0\">Notice what is <b>not</b> said</li><li class=\"d1\">not \"silly superstition\", not \"Torah doesn't say that\", not \"don't worry how you kill\"</li><li class=\"d1\">said: calling unclean what <b>God has made clean</b></li><li class=\"d1\"><b>wasn't always clean, is now</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Q: permission? - <b>no</b>: <b>something has changed</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not that the rule doesn't apply: Paul later quotes <b>Leviticus</b>, \"<b>touch no unclean thing</b>\"</li><li class=\"d1\">still wrong to be unclean; what <b>is and isn't unclean</b> has changed</li></ul>"},{"t":2357.24,"lv":3,"h":"Clean and unclean: camp and world","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">OT <b>clean vs unclean animals</b></li><li class=\"d1\">clean = <b>domesticated</b>, kept in camp, raised for food</li><li class=\"d1\">unclean = <b>wild, scavengers</b>, outside the camp</li><li class=\"d1\">(<b>Leviticus</b>: owl, nighthawk, sparrow unclean birds)</li><li class=\"d0\"><b>Camp</b> = where Israel lives, <b>God dwells in the tabernacle</b> - kept clean</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>Ananias and Sapphira</b>: wicked in God's presence = dangerous</li><li class=\"d1\">rest of the world = <b>unclean</b>, under sin and the devil</li><li class=\"d1\">John: Satan <b>prince of this world</b></li></ul>"},{"t":2455.26,"lv":2,"h":"Christ rules the whole world","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">What changed: Christ <b>crucified and risen</b></li><li class=\"d1\">defeated <b>death, sin, hell, Satan</b></li><li class=\"d1\">who rules now? <b>Jesus</b> - whole world, <b>not just the camp</b>, Jerusalem, Jews</li><li class=\"d1\"><b>no outside of his kingdom</b> anymore</li><li class=\"d1\">whole <b>material creation is clean</b> - that's the vision</li></ul>"},{"t":2515.07,"lv":3,"h":"Why the vision, why now","b":"<ul><li class=\"d0\">Who is on the way to Peter? <b>Gentiles</b>, to invite a <b>Jew into a Gentile's house</b></li><li class=\"d1\">not just Gentile - a <b>Roman</b>, \"really Gentile Gentile\"</li><li class=\"d1\">Gentiles = <b>unclean</b>, of Satan, to the Jews</li><li class=\"d0\">Vision uses <b>animals</b> but is about <b>the whole world and creation</b></li><li class=\"d1\">no person outside <b>Christ's reign</b>, ascended and <b>enthroned</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"may not be loyal subjects\" - <b>still their Lord</b>, like it or not</li><li class=\"d1\">-> <b>no person is unclean</b></li><li class=\"d0\">Object lesson: do something <b>horribly unclean</b> to prepare you for <b>something you'll think is unclean</b></li><li class=\"d1\">\"since God has made this man Cornelius clean, <b>don't you dare call him unclean</b>\" or filthy</li></ul>"}]});
